{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 125, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring the direct input-to-output path gives large gains (+6 to +48 on IN16), while replacing an existing conv or pool on edge 3 with skip gives only small gains."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling a missing edge 3 with a conv adds a short path and capacity at once, giving gains of 2 to 78 points, much larger than swapping one op for another on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 3, cutting edge 0 can starve or disconnect the output (-78 on C10 in one case), whereas with edge 3 present the drop is around 1 point."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing an output edge hurts more when the direct path to the output is already missing, because fewer routes are left to carry signal and gradients."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is already gone, removing edge 3 leaves edge 4 as the only output path, which makes the cell much weaker than when edge 5 still feeds the output."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 4 makes up for the missing edge-3 shortcut (+8.2 on IN16), but is mildly harmful when edge 3 already provides a short path (+0.35 / -1.1)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 5 helps deep conv cells that lack the edge-3 shortcut (+7.3 on IN16) and hurts when that shortcut exists."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing the conv on edge 0 with a skip shortens the effective depth, which matters most when there is no edge-3 shortcut (+14 vs +1.6 on IN16, and positive vs negative on C10 and C100)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv has diminishing returns when the cell already convolves on the output edge, compared with conv-poor parents where gains are tens of points."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 4 already provides a conv path through node 1, adding a conv on edge 2 adds little capacity (about 0 to 2 points) compared with conv-poor parents (+6 to +35)."}], "tok": 18321, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none", "nor_co